Argument in Favor of Measure N
Santa Ana families deserve safe parks and playgrounds, quality streets
and infrastructure, and a clean community. We deserve fast emergency
response times from our police officers and firefighters, and we deserve
a good quality of life for our children and seniors-WITHOUT increasing
taxes on our working families.
This is why we encourage you to VOTE YES on this measure to maintain
Santa Ana’s existing tax levels, maintain our streets, public safety, and
essential services.
Passing this ballot measure would:
1. Allow the city to maintain 454 miles of streets, 90 miles of storm
drains, and 371 acres of parks.
2. Keep every dollar raised by this ballot measure here in Santa Ana.
The county, state, and federal governments cannot take it from us.
3. Ensure that we have enough police officers, firefighters, and
paramedics to respond to 911 calls.
4. NOT increase taxes. It only maintains the tax rate approved by
voters in 2018.
5. Require a committee of local residents to oversee the use of these
local tax dollars.
Many other Orange County cities have similar provisions in place without
a sunset, including Westminster, Buena Park, Garden Grove, La Habra,
Placentia, Seal Beach, and Los Alamitos.
Without the passage of this ballot measure, we may not have enough first
responders necessary to keep our community safe, we will have to make
tough decisions regarding maintaining streets and parks, and our working
families, seniors, and children will not get the quality of life Santa Ana
residents deserve.
A YES VOTE protects our streets, parks, public safety staffing levels, and
essential services.
A YES VOTE will protect Santa Ana’s future.
